    "extraction": {
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2 : Overview of the proposed AVA-VLA framework. At each timestep, the recurrent state is projected from the previous hidden state to preserve historical context and to initialize the current action tokens. Then the AVA module combines this recurrent state with text-conditioned visual features from the current observation to generate soft importance scores, which modulate the visual attention matrices throughout the backbone LLM, enabling the model to focus on task-relevant regions based on both temporal context and current perception.",
      "image_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2511.18960v4/AVA.png",
